  English (United States) — the source catalogue for the Windows app (#91).

  Two kinds of key:
    * "Uid.Property" keys are resolved by XAML through x:Uid. Attached properties
      use the "[using:Namespace]Class.Property" form.
    * Plain keys are read from code through the generated Strings class
      (tools/gen_strings.py → Strings.g.cs). "{0}"-style placeholders become
      method arguments; a placeholder may carry a format such as {0:F1}.

  Every other language mirrors these keys exactly; StringCatalogueTests fails the
  build when one drifts. Vocabulary lives in docs/localisation-glossary.md.
-->
